<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Not only my lamp, Lord, but my vessel too,</l><l>Redeeming the time to be filled up with You.</l><l>I’m going forth to meet You, my Bridegroom so dear.</l><l>I know then at midnight You’ll soon, Lord, appear.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Lord, make us ready at any cost</l><l>Or else at Your coming we’ll suffer great loss.</l><l>We don’t want to say, Lord, our lamp’s going out.</l><l>Then it is too late when we hear the great shout.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>As virgins we’re loving and enjoying You,</l><l>Always responding, You’re fresh and so new.</l><l>Our spirits You’re filling and soul saturating.</l><l>Our lamps and our vessels we surrender to You.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
